course: dictionary
lesson: 549
title: Attend: go, care, or pay attention
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Attend has three main meanings, and the words around it show you which one to use. To attend something is to go to it and be there, such as school, a meeting or a party. To attend to someone or something is to look after them or deal with them.
explain: Read the clues. «Attend school» and «attend a meeting» are about going somewhere. «Attend to a wound» is about treating an injury. Ask yourself: is someone going somewhere, caring for something, or listening?
explain: The third meaning is to pay attention. The Mouse in Alice says, «You are not attending!», which means Alice is not listening. Alice mishears «I had not!» as «a knot», which shows what happens when you are not paying attention.
fact: Attend means to go to something and be there, like a lesson, an assembly or a concert.
fact: Attend to means to deal with something or look after someone, as in «attend to a wound».
fact: Attend can also mean to pay attention, as in «You are not attending!»
fact: Schools keep an attendance register to record which pupils are there each day.
fact: Look-alike words can trick you: in French, attendre looks like attend but means to wait.
exercise: Pupils must «attend school» every day. What does attend mean here? | To be given a prize for school | To sleep through the lessons | *To go to school and be there | To tidy up after school
exercise: The nurse must «attend to the wound» on Sam's knee. What does attend to mean? | To count how many cuts there are | To paint the knee bright red | To ignore it and walk away | *To look after it and treat it
exercise: The Mouse cries, «You are not attending!» What does attending mean here? | Going to a party | Writing a letter | Waiting for a bus | *Paying attention and listening
test: Maya did not attend school on Monday. What does attend mean? | *Went to school and was there | Ate lunch at home | Was given a reward | Painted the classroom
test: Asha asked her friend to attend to the lost dog until its owner came. What does attend to mean? | Draw a picture of it | Forget about it | Race after it | *Look after it and take care of it
exam: In French, attendre looks like attend. What does it mean? | To listen carefully | To look after someone | *To wait | To go to school
